    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53204" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καππαδόκαι</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶν</span>,
			οἱ, <u>Cappadocians</u>, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			5.49
		</span></i>, etc.:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καππάδοκες</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ων</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			6.4.2
		</span></i>, etc.:—fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καππαδόκισσα</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Id.
			14.2.17
		</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καππαδοκία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ, <u>Cappadocia</u>, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			1.71
		</span></i>, etc.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καππαδοκίζω</span></b> ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>favour the
			Cappadocians</i>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Mith.</u>
				53
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be Cappadocianized</i> (with pun on Joannes
			Cappadox), [<i><span class="en">
				Demod.
			</span></i>]<i><span class="en">
				5
			</span></i>.</div>
